<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Cairns hike planner" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
  <metadata>
    <name>Little Bandera Mountain</name>
    <desc>Ira Spring trailhead to Little Bandera and back. 10.6 km, +919 m, −919 m.</desc>
  </metadata>
  <wpt lat="47.424736" lon="-121.583505">
    <ele>655.8</ele>
    <name>1 Ira Spring trailhead</name>
    <desc>Northwest Forest Pass (or an Interagency pass) on the dashboard. Vault toilet, no water. The last miles of FR 9031 are potholed gravel; the lot fills early on summer and autumn weekends. Carry 2 L each: the creek near the start is the only water.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
    <type>Milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.422657" lon="-121.576638">
    <ele>790.5</ele>
    <name>2 Old Mason Lake Trail junction</name>
    <desc>The old trail splits off here; stay on the Ira Spring Trail. So far it has been an old roadbed at a steady 10–13%, past the Mason Creek crossing.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
    <type>Milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.417504" lon="-121.561676">
    <ele>1000.8</ele>
    <name>3 Out of the trees, 1,000 m</name>
    <desc>Switchbacks on the open south slope: beargrass, huckleberries and the I-90 valley below. Hot in afternoon sun, no shade until the top. Eat now.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
    <type>Milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.418600" lon="-121.556556">
    <ele>1266.6</ele>
    <name>4 Bandera Mountain Trail junction</name>
    <desc>Leave the Ira Spring Trail (it carries on to Mason Lake) and turn right, straight up the ridge. The last 0.9 km climbs 310 m: steep, rocky, with talus near the top. Poles out.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
    <type>Milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.418110" lon="-121.547678">
    <ele>1575.1</ele>
    <name>5 Little Bandera summit</name>
    <desc>Rainier to the south, Mason Lake and the lakes basin below to the north, Kaleetan and Chair Peak beyond. The true Bandera summit is about 1 km east along the ridge (+60 m, boulder hopping, harder coming back). Skip it when wet, icy or short of time.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
    <type>Milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.418600" lon="-121.556556">
    <ele>1266.6</ele>
    <name>6 Bandera junction (down)</name>
    <desc>Back on the Ira Spring Trail: go left, downhill. The branch climbing ahead goes to Mason Lake. The steep pitch above is where knees and ankles suffer; slow is fine.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
    <type>Milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.417504" lon="-121.561676">
    <ele>1000.8</ele>
    <name>7 Into the trees (down)</name>
    <desc>Shade again. The rest is a steady, gentle descent on the old roadbed.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
    <type>Milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.424736" lon="-121.583505">
    <ele>655.8</ele>
    <name>8 Ira Spring trailhead</name>
    <desc>Finish. Back at the car.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
    <type>Milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <trk>
    <name>Little Bandera Mountain</name>
